      "devanagari": "क्रुद्धम् निःश्वसमानम् तम् प्रदीप्तम् इव तेजसा |\nभ्रातुर् व्यसन संतप्तम् दृष्ट्वा दशरथ आत्मजम्\nउत्पपात हरिश्रेष्ठो हित्वा सौवर्णम् आसनम् |\nमहान् महेन्द्रस्य यथा स्वलंकृत इव ध्वजः",
      "iast": "kruddham niḥśvasamānam tam pradīptam iva tejasā |\nbhrātur vyasana saṃtaptam dṛṣṭvā daśaratha ātmajam\nut.hpapāta hariśreṣṭho hitvā sauvarṇam āsanam |\nmahān mahendrasya yathā svalaṃkṛta iva dhvajaḥ",
      "translation": "On seeing Lakshmana, the son of Dasharatha, who is exasperated and exhaling heavily, and who searing in the anguish of his brother is flaring up like a firestorm, Sugreeva hopped up from his golden seat and tottered like the highly decorated flagstaff of Indra, which will be wobbly before it is thrown to ground after the ritual.",
