      "label": "4.34.9",
      "numbers": [
        9
      ],
      "devanagari": "शतम् अश्व अनृते हन्ति सहस्रम् तु गव अनृते |\nआत्मानम् स्व जनम् हन्ति पुरुषः पुरुष अनृते",
      "iast": "śatam aśva anṛte hanti sahasram tu gava anṛte |\nātmānam sva janam hanti puruṣaḥ puruṣa anṛte",
      "translation": "\"A person gets attached to the sin of killing of a hundred of his manes, deified souls of his own ancestors, if he promises to gift one horse but fails to do so, and in promising to gift one cow but failing in it he gets the sin of killing a thousand manes, and if he promises to a person to do the needful help and fails in rendering that help, then he gets the sin of suicide along with the sin of killing his own kith and kin.",
      "notes": [
        "The above verse will be generally translated as 'A person gets attached to the sin of killing of a hundred horses if he promises to gift one horse but fails to do so, and in promising to gift one cow but failing in it he gets the sin of killing a thousand cows, and if he belies to a person to do the needful help, he then gets the sin of killing himself along with his own kith and kin...' But, it is not the sin of killing hundred horses or thousand cows, but it the sin of killing those many numbers of killer's manes, the deified souls of one's own dead ancestors. This is as per Manu dharma and it is detailed in Dharmaakuutam as:",
        "<em>atra aśva viṣaye anṛtam vaktā sva pūrva puruṣāṇām śatam hanti - svargāt pracyavya narakam tiryak yonim vā prāpayati - gava anṛte sahasram sva pūrva puruṣām tathā karoti - puruṣa viṣaye anṛte sa bāndhavaḥ svayam eva narakam tiryak yoni vā prāpnoti iti uktam - - mānave - - yāvato bāndhavān asmin hanti sākṣe anṛtam vadan - - panca paśva anṛtam hanti daśa hanti gava anṛte - - dk</em>& and he goes on quoting Prahlaada and Dudhanva discussion in Maha Bharata, Udyoga parva. Killing the already dead souls is lesser sin than the killing of living beings and committing suicide."
      ],
